ting assets with a gross capacity of approximately 2.0 gigawatt (GW) and has investments in generating assets with approximately 0.3 GW of net generation capacity. It generates and sells hydroelectric energy in Canada, and capacity and renewable attributes are produced by its portfolio of 14 hydroelectric power generation facilities located in the provinces of Alberta, Ontario, New Brunswick, and Quebec. As of December 31, 2025, it had a combined gross generating capacity of approximately 112 megawatts (MW) and a combined net generating capacity of approximately 105 MW. The company was formerly known as Traduction Militech Translation Inc. in October 2009. The company was incorporated in 1988 and is headquartered in Oakville, Canada.", "sector": "Utilities", "industry": "Utilities - Diversified"}, "valuation": {"pe": 23.108109, "pb": 1.0351944, "ps": 2.5973477, "roe": 2.67, "net_margin": 6.72, "debt_to_equity": 133.219, "div_yield": 4.15, "rev_growth": 14.4, "market_cap": 6580640256.0, "forward_pe": 14.946222, "peg": null, "payout": 100.19, "five_yr_yield": 6.14, "pe_sector_med": 26.066666, "pb_sector_med": 2.49494, "roe_sector_med": 3.02, "div_yield_sector_med": 3.27}, "archetype": "mixed", "archetype_label": "Mixed profile", "archetype_label_zh": "\u6df7\u5408\u7279\u5f81", "consensus": {"n_analysts": 3, "target_mean": 10.011497, "target_high": 10.398524, "target_low": 9.267262, "rating_mean": 2.58333, "rating": "Hold", "rating_zh": "\u6301\u6709", "upside_pct": 17.1}, "positioning": {"shares_short": 19472767.0, "days_to_cover": 7.13, "short_pct_float": null, "held_insiders": 0.03, "held_institutions": 73.9}}, "earnings": {"next_date": "2026-08-07", "surprises": [{"date": "2026-05-08", "eps": 0.13, "est": 0.11, "surprise_pct": 13.3}, {"date": "2026-03-06", "eps": 0.06, "est": 0.05, "surprise_pct": 30.1}, {"date": "2025-11-07", "eps": 0.09, "est": 0.06, "surprise_pct": 41.9}, {"date": "2025-08-08", "eps": 0.04, "est": 0.04, "surprise_pct": 0.9}]}, "factor_beta": {"